    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "description",
      "value": "In general, legal systems can be split between civil law and common law systems. Modern scholars argue that the significance of this distinction has progressively declined. The numerous legal transplants, typical of modern law, result in the sharing of many features traditionally associated with either common law or civil law. The third type of legal system is religious law, based on scriptures.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0006",
        "chunk_title": "Legal systems",
        "chunk_order": 5,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "determinants",
      "value": "The specific system by which a country is ruled is often determined by its history, its connections with other countries, or its adherence to international standards.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0006",
        "chunk_title": "Legal systems",
        "chunk_order": 5,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "defining_features",
      "value": "The sources that jurisdictions adopt as authoritatively binding are the defining features of any legal system.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0006",
        "chunk_title": "Legal systems",
        "chunk_order": 5,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "overview",
      "field": "definition",
      "value": "Civil law is the legal system used in most countries around the world today.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0007",
        "chunk_title": "Civil law",
        "chunk_order": 6,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "overview",
      "field": "sources",
      "value": "The primary authoritative sources are legislation, especially codifications in constitutions or statutes passed by government, and custom.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0007",
        "chunk_title": "Civil law",
        "chunk_order": 6,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "overview",
      "field": "historical_example",
      "value": "An early example of codifications is the Babylonian Codex Hammurabi.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
